# Vaulter AI — credentials template
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# This file is safe to commit — it never holds a real secret, only
# placeholders. setup_wizard.py copies it to confidentials/.env (which
# IS gitignored) the first time someone runs the wizard on a machine
# that doesn't have one yet.
#
# FOR YASHU / IT — READ THIS ONCE:
# There are no API keys. Nothing in this file is required, and a completely
# blank .env is a working setup. Document search is local, ranking is
# arithmetic, ground truth and proximity come from free public data, and the
# qualitative read happens in the Claude conversation that asked for it.
#
# What remains below is only for machines where OneDrive put a folder somewhere
# unexpected, or that should track the canary release channel.
#
# Do NOT commit this file after filling in real values — copy it to
# confidentials/.env.template.filled (or wherever your distribution
# process pulls from) and keep that copy out of git, exactly like
# confidentials/.env itself already is.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where the firm's document library is synced, if OneDrive put it
# somewhere other than the auto-detected default. Leave blank normally.
VAULTER_CORPUS_DIR=

# Just the FOLDER NAME of the firm's document library inside your OneDrive
# (not a full path -- use VAULTER_CORPUS_DIR above for that). Leave blank
# normally: the library is found automatically by its shape, since OneDrive
# names a synced SharePoint library "<Org> - <Site>" while every personal
# folder (Desktop, Documents, Pictures) is a plain single name.
#
# Usually unnecessary even with several libraries synced: the one holding the
# team's "Vaulter AI Shared" folder is recognised automatically.
#
# Only fill this in if you sync MORE THAN ONE SharePoint library AND none of
# them has that folder yet, in which
# case the system refuses to guess between them and says so on startup.
# The name is kept here rather than in the code on purpose -- the code is
# published publicly, and a library's display name identifies the firm's
# SharePoint site.
VAULTER_CORPUS_SUBFOLDER=

# A distinctive WORD from the library's folder name, if the full name differs
# from machine to machine but always contains the same word. Only consulted
# when several libraries are synced and none can be identified by its contents.
# Left blank here on purpose -- this file is public, so put the word in your own
# confidentials/.env rather than here.
VAULTER_CORPUS_HINT=

# Where the team's shared Vaulter output folder lives, if it isn't the
# auto-detected default. Leave blank normally.
VAULTER_SHARED_DIR=

# Auto-update channel (optional, defaults to "general" if left blank).
# Leave this blank/unset on every normal staff machine. Only set it to
# "canary" on a small number of designated machines (e.g. the
# maintainer's own) that should pick up a newly-published version
# immediately, before it's confirmed healthy and promoted to everyone
# else — see release.py and CLAUDE.md's "Auto-update" section.
VAULTER_UPDATE_CHANNEL=
